e":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"84ceb6c6dd85bfe2896d593694367c72f65f0cb0970e31bc9c423565b95ea8ef","compact":"989a75ef578cf32f17c28c9b36569af585af69a00b995f313a769069b01748a1","nasal":"d497a12ce4a98ffb342e20d4c77f9ea6eb3e269e05e0d6a2912d332d3fdb5e23"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-2-7","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":2,"verse":7,"english":"All these heroes, these leaders of monkeyhordes, who are ardent for they welfare, are competent to enter into fire itself. From their cheerful attitude I know this, and firm is my faith.","alignment":{"type":"grouped","confidence":0.871,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-2-7"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6002007","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"f732b4b02183bea829b4a8a9d470b18222839a6cb698eeb6a974b70dd6492c3f","compact":"722325c4e2baeb456b2bce70a3ed7b9b6e415568af043d76b123ae356d898ce4","nasal":"722325c4e2baeb456b2bce70a3ed7b9b6e415568af043d76b123ae356d898ce4"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-2-8","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":2,"verse":8,"english":"All these heroes, these leaders of monkeyhordes, who are ardent for they welfare, are competent to enter into fire itself. From their cheerful attitude I know this, and firm is my faith. It behove you so to arrange things that, slaying the foe, Rāvana of impious acts, we may bring higher Sītā by our own prowess.","alignment":{"type":"split","confidence":0.446,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-2-7","DUTT-6-2-8"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6002008","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"3828202f4b1d35dc93d2e7d8c36f9f5210dcda47071eb90a3bf272c3ca304c4c","compact":"e223885f25347fc71491ac808b9f4889fa4fb37a485ba75d13e893fc8884fa7d","nasal":"bb6d23c83671416fffcaed35536d339b0044ee09e2086762adfa582b0a87cfe5"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-2-9","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":2,"verse":9,"english":"Do you, O Rāghava, so order matters that a bridge may be constructed (over the main), and that we may behold the palace of the Rākşasa monarch.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.867,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-2-9"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6002009","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"ec320bdf012b4b73b5cadf2467aed1f50d5e5da9df7380712c06aadd6f4b16f3","compact":"d9cc6279e09a5a46f25bd96338a9608725b0ea889d9577052adf2f21e6a55f4f","nasal":"d9cc6279e09a5a46f25bd96338a9608725b0ea889d9577052adf2f21e6a55f4f"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-2-10","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":2,"verse":10,"english":"We having seen the city of Lankā, established on the summit of Triküța, do you for certain conclude Răvaņa as slain in battle immediately after (we see her).","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.908,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-2-10"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6002010","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"1fd8a05c33fcc957ab0dc421c76f8245d77ce21c29d574621cc01b088a11ceef","compact":"3eabf6cee841b18efd160e3d44432ad6798cacce8b1e77b2d09a6f1ddfd1cb87","nasal":"2e75c354a587b168fc80257aaeeb67427529b5514f2a28f6b05ded75f6901229"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-2-11","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":2,"verse":11,"english":"When the bridge over the ocean has been constructed up to near Laňkä, and when my forces have crossed (over the sea), consider victory as secured. As these monkeys are heroic in fight, and able to wear forms at will, O king, do not let your intellect get stupefied and thus mar all interests. In this world, sorrow berefts people of their prowess.","alignment":{"type":"grouped","confidence":0.677,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-2-12"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6002011","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"792d343d84b92411190c61e0e6a609e1c2bdf46587c714f4cdc777892ac99f7a","compact":"132eb1acf4bbc988044c0e921dd5a6816b10bbc96d24bb10b8b126e62855c501","nasal":"d539ff4374c26cbdc75207f3d2a2104b390b9ac65251581b768be2c057ae5d51"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-2-12","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":2,"verse":12,"english":"When the bridge over the ocean has been constructed up to near Laňkä, and when my forces have crossed (over the sea), consider victory as secured. As these monkeys are heroic in fight, and able to wear forms at will, O king, do not let your intellect get stupefied and thus mar all interests. In this world, sorrow berefts people of their prowess.","alignment":{"type":"grouped","confidence":0.556,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-2-12"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6002012","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"e1befd5dbb42bdd23d12aa359a20c07197fb29d3ff35169fe44fcef7a792fbd8","compact":"c685475bebc7c24bc7579db73270a00232cc8c9a3513ed14afbbac279e7523c2","nasal":"c685475bebc7c24bc7579db73270a00232cc8c9a3513ed14afbbac279e7523c2"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-2-13","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":2,"verse":13,"english":"At this time, O eminently wise one, do you realise goodness through they energy.* Of heroic, high-souled, men like yourself, on their sustaining and entire or a partial loss, grief undo every interest. *i.e. as I understand this rather obscure passage, prove the good through your vigour-secure victory to the cause of goodness through they might.","alignment":{"type":"grouped","confidence":0.327,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-2-14"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6002013","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"83d3a6a01d9ec625435cf54d28074919fdff51e2cfb0c453b8ffeb26ca6fda86","compact":"abe0ebb18a5852ba06bf0e234effe0014ec573c3e556fd37755b6af9d68b6df4","nasal":"bcb2f579b4310909a2efda680f4cd8f29a84ebbe0e4e2c688597ec1042f932f6"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-2-14","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":2,"verse":14,"english":"At this time, O eminently wise one, do you realise goodness through they energy.* Of heroic, high-souled, men like yourself, on their sustaining and entire or a partial loss, grief undo every interest. *i.e. as I understand this rather obscure passage, prove the good through your vigour-secure victory to the cause of goodness through they might. Therefore, the foremost of intelligent persons, and conversant with every lore, you should along with councillors like me, strive to beat they foe.","alignment":{"type":"split","confidence":0.392,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-2-14","DUTT-6-2-15"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6002014","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"eb06de2167dd422f82caf9931ab973e220d17375dfa8670ce7a1eb2aba78a94b","compact":"eb2b0485eaed0a430f7e15101888a9906a0bca955f0614cf85f77fa82f50dff5","nasal":"eb2b0485eaed0a430f7e15101888a9906a0bca955f0614cf85f77fa82f50dff5"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-2-15","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":2,"verse":15,"english":"Find I none in the three worlds, O Rāghava, who can stay in fight before you equipped with your bow,","alignment":{"type":"grouped","confidence":0.328,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-2-16"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6002015","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"af0977180bacdb541a466488132e13fad2720e1c7cc166ab9b370fc5626b8ca3","compact":"cfe6e4a32543b2ef37d1b12950cb4ad8143f8bde7fdf594c06d55ab2e1471d0a","nasal":"cfe6e4a32543b2ef37d1b12950cb4ad8143f8bde7fdf594c06d55ab2e1471d0a"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-2-16","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":2,"verse":16,"english":"Find I none in the three worlds, O Rāghava, who can stay in fight before you equipped with your bow, Your business entrusted to these monkeys shall not (anyway) suffer. And soon, crossing over the boundless main, you shall behold Sītā.","alignment":{"type":"split","confidence":0.414,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-2-16","DUTT-6-2-17"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6002016","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"3f81895a5758b43019ab51ae4502c4ea29e96a23cb3fb5772ae618ed5b92734e","compact":"978fd3c7940f1aaede9654dfc9f1fa068d9bf32e8aaeab8a777dbcb5968dce12","nasal":"978fd3c7940f1aaede9654dfc9f1fa068d9bf32e8aaeab8a777dbcb5968dce12"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-2-17","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":2,"verse":17,"english":"Your business entrusted to these monkeys shall not (anyway) suffer. And soon, crossing over the boundless main, you shall behold Sītā. Therefore, O king, renounce your sorrow, and call up wrath. Those Ksatriyas that conceive no anger in respect of their enemies, have their activity annulled; and all fear furious persons.","alignment":{"type":"split","confidence":0.369,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-2-17","DUTT-6-2-18"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6002017","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"695a0719bcbf2f59278ab238d4f841ad97f425aabb043325478f6bcf415e27c5","compact":"27de57287677878f51b58c6059ca90cb7739ca542f9699c0f9f1756c492f23d7","nasal":"0be3f0cc6d14eba3d14b68c559e654c96f5daa0dc9797c6355620bdd0377f51b"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-2-18","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":2,"verse":18,"english":"Therefore, O king, renounce your sorrow, and call up wrath. Those Ksatriyas that conceive no anger in respect of their enemies, have their activity annulled; and all fear furious persons. Drawing nigh to us, do you, gifted with acute intelligence, cast about for crossing over the dreadful deep, lord of streams, along with us.","alignment":{"type":"split","confidence":0.535,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-2-18","DUTT-6-2-19"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6002018","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"a17a4a469d677813944f4e320aff27a72714d7cff05ef3f6373ffe7d53fe8190","compact":"9e1e058a14ebe2f3affcc6f7b3ae4f262cafb1e89728e933f2b8aeb88f644c99","nasal":"a85b5ffbc0559623eca4084a88dc0d9885b5d0b90a0622cc423de18a05c1bcee"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-2-19","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":2,"verse":19,"english":"Drawing nigh to us, do you, gifted with acute intelligence, cast about for crossing over the dreadful deep, lord of streams, along with us.","alignment":{"type":"grouped","confidence":0.544,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-2-19"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6002019","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"3c8438123b2654727801320eb665d8609a264e60c9af3246ddbea52cbe17f66b","compact":"09107f7558f92048f15e01847d5d4063d0c00455f490309c8de1ae429011a3c7","nasal":"09107f7558f92048f15e01847d5d4063d0c00455f490309c8de1ae429011a3c7"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-2-20","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":2,"verse":20,"english":"These monkeys, heroic and capable of assuming in fight forms at will, shall slaughter those foes by showering rocks and trees.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.475,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-2-21"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6002020","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"f06a9f23550c64eaa87cac265f79c4d805b18d8ca550d14798d67fe6ce3e2975","compact":"838ef4cffb69f1d9563b07b6c8642584999b0bf4cc699f91baa24f912876ed7f","nasal":"e40fbb7a34d2235ed012e621ddfa224ac5ae50f05b0ae6720298bb0f3ea1133c"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-2-21","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":2,"verse":21,"english":"And what is the use of dilating? Every way you shall prove victorious. And I see omens, and my mind is filled with delight.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-2-23"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6002021","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"a27ee110f4eb79cc66e48b75ca8fcbee6e02902430e47bd0b3f8177563ace1bb","compact":"7428b3cd9aef8ac54ad3aceb98ae0b27c2a83dbdf953dafcf348e7a2dc45bda0","nasal":"7428b3cd9aef8ac54ad3aceb98ae0b27c2a83dbdf953dafcf348e7a2dc45bda0"}}]
